# EPL Value Betting & Corner Recommender System

## Project Overview
This project predicts Premier League match outcomes, goal distributions, and corner counts using statistical models (Dixon-Coles Poisson model) and identifies Value Bets by comparing model probabilities against bookmaker odds.

## Tech Stack
- **Language**: Python 3.10+
- **Data & Math**: Pandas, NumPy, SciPy (`scipy.optimize.minimize`), Statsmodels
- **UI Framework**: Streamlit
- **Data Source**: Direct CSV download from `football-data.co.uk`

## Core Domain Logic
1. **Dixon-Coles Model**:
   - Predicts goals for Home (\(X\)) and Away (\(Y\)) teams using attack/defense strengths and home advantage (\(\gamma\)).
   - Uses tau adjustment \(\tau(x, y)\) for low scores (0-0, 1-0, 0-1, 1-1) with parameter \(\rho\).
2. **Value Betting Engine**:
   - Fair Odds = \(1 / P_{\text{model}}\)
   - Expected Value (\(\text{EV}\)) = \((P_{\text{model}} \times \text{Odds}_{\text{bookmaker}}) - 1\)
   - Recommend bet ONLY when \(\text{EV} \ge 0.05\) (\(5\%\)).
3. **Corner Prediction**:
   - Poisson regression based on 3-season home/away corner stats (`HC`, `AC`).

## Coding Conventions
- Use clean, modular Python functions with Type Hints.
- Document functions using Docstrings describing math parameters (e.g., \(\lambda\), \(\mu\), \(\rho\)).
- Keep Streamlit UI logic (`app.py`) separate from statistical calculation modules (`src/`).